~ first_night_alone  

me: …It’s way too quiet.  

me: Every little sound feels [b]ten times[/b] louder. Was that the fridge… or a serial killer?  

me: I should be sleeping, but my brain has decided to overanalyze [b]everything[/b].  

me: Maybe I just need some background noise… or to curl up under the blankets and pretend I’m not here.  

me: …Yeah, that sounds like a solid plan.  
do Global.player.decrement_gauge(25 , "energy")  
do Global.player.increment_gauge(20 , "stress")  

=> END  

~ strange_noise_night  

me: …What was that sound?  

me: It came from outside… or was it just the wind?  

me: Maybe I’m just imagining things. It’s probably nothing.  

me: But... what if it’s something important? Should I check?  

- Check it out
	me: Alright, fine. I’ll get up and check.  
	I get out of bed and move toward the noise.  
	I bump into the table and stumble, but catch myself.  
	me: Ouch, that hurt.  
	I reach the window and look outside.  
	me: …Oh, it’s just the wind. What a shocker.    
	do Global.player.decrement_gauge(20 , "moral")  


- Stay in bed 
	me: Nah, I’m not going anywhere. If something bad happens, at least I’ll be [b]comfy[/b] when it happens.
	do Global.player.decrement_gauge(25 , "energy")  
	do Global.player.increment_gauge(25 , "stress")  

=> END  

~ dad_call

You wake up in the middle of the night, you notice missed calls from your father
An air of panic takes over your body

- Try to call him
	me: Okay, calm down. He’s probably just trying to reach me for something important.  
	me: I dial the number quickly, hoping it’s nothing serious.  
	[b]Phone rings...[/b] 
	me: Come on, pick up... 
	[b]No answer[/b]
	me: Why isn't he picking up? This isn’t like him…  
	do Global.player.decrement_gauge(20 , "moral")  
	do Global.player.increment_gauge(15 , "stress")  


- Call my mother instead
	me: Maybe I should call Mom first. She’ll know what’s going on.  
	me: I quickly dial her number, hoping she’s already in the loop.  
	[b]Phone rings...[/b]
	mom: Hey sweetie, what's wrong?  
	me: Hi Mom, I saw missed calls from Dad, is everything okay?  
	mom: Oh, don’t worry! He’s fine. He just found that old thing you were looking for—the one you thought you lost! He’s been trying to get a hold of you to tell you.  
	me: Wait, really? That’s a relief!  
	mom: Yeah, he’s super excited to give it to you. I’ll let him know you called.  
	do Global.player.increment_gauge(10 , "moral")  


=> END

~ noisy_neighbors  

me: …Are they serious right now?  
me: It’s the middle of the night, and they’re acting like it’s a [b]music festival[/b].  
me: I could try to ignore it… or do something about it.  

- Bang on the wall  
	me: That’s it. I’ve had enough.  
	[b]THUMP THUMP THUMP![/b]  
	…Silence.
	me: Did it work?  
	[b]Loud music resumes, even louder than before.[/b]  
	me: Great. That totally backfired.  
	do Global.player.decrement_gauge(15 , "moral")  
	do Global.player.increment_gauge(20 , "stress")  

- Try to sleep anyway  
	me: Maybe if I just focus really hard on sleeping, I can tune it out…  
	I bury my face in my pillow and hope for the best.  
	me: …It’s not working. At all.  
	me: This is going to be a [b]loooooong[/b] night.  
	do Global.player.decrement_gauge(30 , "energy")  
	do Global.player.decrement_gauge(10 , "moral")  

- Put on headphones  
	me: Fine, if I can’t make them shut up, I’ll just block them out.  
	me: I put on my headphones and blast white noise to drown them out.  
	me: It’s not perfect, but at least I might get some sleep.  
	do Global.player.decrement_gauge(15 , "energy")  
	do Global.player.increment_gauge(5 , "stress")  

=> END  
